fact WorkItem(id: "WI-611", description: some(value: "Typer: refine a SELF-RETURNING spec op's carrier to the receiver's CONCRETE provider WITHOUT changing the op functor — the enabler for NESTED container [simp]-law firing (WI-596 follow-up). WI-596 delivered the requires-guard mechanism (simp_guard_holds_core keys on the carrier arg's type), but the stdlib Set/Map laws are NESTED — member(?x, insert(?s,?x)) <=> true, union(?s, empty()) <=> ?s, get(put(?m,?k,?v),?k) <=> some(?v) — so the carrier argument is a spec-op subterm (insert/put/empty) whose DECLARED return is the ABSTRACT sort (Set/Map). On a freestanding redex value_type_term reads that abstract Set, sort_provides(Set,Set) is non-reflexive, so the guard SUSPENDS (sound, never NAF-decides) and the nested laws stay dormant. There is a genuine CATCH-22 (documented in wi596_container_guard_test.rs): keep the spec functor so the law's inner pattern (Set.insert) matches -> the subterm types abstract -> guard fails; OR override the op on the provider to refine its return to the concrete carrier -> the subterm functor becomes ConcreteBag.insert -> the Set.insert-keyed law can no longer match. Plus provider-completeness (WI-363) requires backing the non-law ops once you override any. FIX DIRECTION: when a spec op's return type IS the enclosing sort (a self-return, insert(s: Set, x: T) -> Set) and the receiver's carrier is a concrete PROVIDER of that sort, refine the op's INFERRED return type to the provider carrier WHILE KEEPING the spec functor (carrier-aware self-return refinement; cf WI-350 carrier-aware dispatch, WI-461 bare-self-receiver identity, WI-374 member-tie). Then member(x, insert(concreteBag, x)) types its carrier arg as concreteBag, sort_provides(concreteBag, Bag) holds, and the nested law fires — no override, no completeness collision. RELATED (same typer spec-op return-grounding family, but those thread the ELEMENT/EFFECT params, not the carrier/self sort): WI-606, WI-608. ACCEPTANCE: a nested container law (member(?x, insert(?s,?x)) <=> true [simp]) on a self-representing sort FIRES over a concrete provider whose ops are NOT all overridden (revive the removed nested test in wi596_container_guard_test.rs); the flat WI-596 tests still pass; cargo-test green. Rust-only (typer)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-596"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-01T12:10:40Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-611", name: "wi502")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-611", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED + pushed main (9b03fc14). FIX: new self_return_spec_op_result_type in typing.rs — when a BODY-LESS spec op's declared return IS its enclosing (self) sort and its self-receiver arg's already-computed type is a CONCRETE provider of that sort, the result carrier IS the receiver carrier (insert(intBag,x):IntBag, not abstract Bag), refined WITHOUT changing the spec functor so the inner law pattern still matches. Gated inside the NON-constructor branch of constructor_value_type (entity_field_types==None), so the common constructor path never pays the operation-info scan; refinement flows via value_type_term into the resolver's simp_requires_guard_holds, so kb.simplify(member(5,insert(ibag,5))) fires member_insert. Reads receiver-carrier authoritatively (result of a self-return IS the receiver), gated on carrier!=spec_sort && sort_provides(carrier,spec) so abstract receivers keep the declared self sort and non-providers are never refined. TESTS (revived nested, wi596_container_guard_test.rs): nested_container_law_fires_over_provider (fires over IntBag) + nested_container_law_does_not_fire_when_carrier_lacks_spec (suspends over Plain). GOTCHA: WI-363 completeness forces the provider to BACK the body-less insert — done via IntBag's OWN insert override (NOT a Bag default, which would make insert non-body-less and defeat the lookup_spec_op_dispatch gate); the LAW op member stays a spec law, matching acceptance's 'ops NOT all overridden'. RESIDUAL: union(?s,empty()) stays bounded — nullary empty() has no receiver to refine from (sort-self grounding, cf WI-608); handles member/insert + get/put only. code-review xhigh: no findings. anthill-core 927/0; workspace green (cli+stl+todo EXIT=0).", at: "2026-07-01T12:11:12Z")
